      "extract": "that, in general, survey respondents do not consider a question on HIV status any more sensitive than several other questions included in bio-behavioural studies on HIV. Inaccuracy of self-reported status Many who believe survey respondents should not be asked to reveal their HIV status also believe that the results of such questioning are likely to be inaccurate because of the effects of social desirability bias",
